# Best-effort common session clock. This component exists only on the well-known
# Bookkeeper session entity (EntityID 0) and only NodeID 0 may modify it.

# session_time is finite, monotonic seconds since session start. Bookkeeper
# SHOULD replace this component approximately once per second. At receipt, a
# peer records local_time_at_receipt from its own monotonic clock and estimates:
#
#   session_now = session_time + (local_now - local_time_at_receipt)
#
# Peers smooth later corrections and MUST NOT expose a session estimate that
# moves backward. Relay latency makes this a coarse clock suitable for ordinary
# animation, audio, and presentation sampling, not precision synchronization.
# It is never used for ECS conflict resolution or message ordering.
pack SessionTimeComponent
- session_time : f64
